From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] test: guards against the categories, not the cases
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The broken call to action passed human review, hosted QA and a whole phase
without being seen. What finds that class of mistake is a test that reads
the source, not a careful reader — so each guard closes a category rather
than the instance that was found.

No fiction: the mocks directory does not exist, the data layer that held it
does not exist, and the four prototype components are gone.

No borrowed identity: no seed tenant name and no literal uuid on any
client-facing surface. The next shortcut will not be called hartmann-social
— it will be an id copied from staging during a debugging session. The
scan deliberately stops before the admin, where an example client name in a
form placeholder is a hint, not data, and where this phase must not reach.

No hand-written project routes: every project-scoped href comes from the
helper, and the attention source is asserted to build its own from the
verified project id.

No parallel authorisation: nothing under the attention domain creates a
Supabase client, names a table or imports the service-role client, and the
guard in its entry point stays outside the error isolation — capturing it
would turn a cross-tenant 404 into a degraded state with the page mounting
over the refusal. A separate case asserts the Next navigation rethrow is
the first statement in the catch, before the log.

No backstage on the client's screen: nothing under the portal or the
components touches the activity log, in any form.

